    field gachaInfo type="[GachaInfoMst]" {
        key "1IR86sAv"
        doc """
        Available summon gates — the same rows GachaList sends.

        Duplicated onto UserInfo because the summon screen paints BEFORE any
        GachaList round trip when the tutorial drives it: tuto15.txt issues
        `change_gacha_top_scene` directly, so SummonsCategorizationScene opens
        with whatever the client already holds.  Sending it only on GachaList
        left GachaInfoList empty and the scene crashed on entry.

        Safe to send from here because GameResponseParser::getResponseObject
        (0x1392568) dispatches this key globally — `1IR86sAv` constructs a
        GachaInfoResponse no matter which handler's payload carries it.
        GachaActionScene and SummonsDetailScene both resolve gates through
        GachaInfoList::getObjectWithGachaID, which this populates.
        """
    }

    field gachaCategories type="[GachaCategory]" {
        key "IBs49NiH"
        doc """
        Summon-screen banner rail — the same rows GachaList sends.

        Same reasoning as gachaInfo above: dispatched globally by
        getResponseObject into a GachaCategoryMstResponse, so it populates
        GachaCategoryMstList regardless of which response carries it, and the
        banner rail is what the tutorial's forced scene change needs present.
        """
    }
}

// ReinforcementInfo is defined in net/reinforcement_info.kdl (xZH6EIQ7 â€” 47
// fields; the local stub here was kept-as-placeholder until the schema was
// decoded).
//
// FriendGetResp emits BOTH wire keys:
//   - xZH6EIQ7 (ReinforcementInfoResponse) â€” populates ReinforcementInfoList,
//     which a captured production response (server/deploy/log_res/2o4axPIC_*.json)
//     confirms is the canonical key the BF server returns here even when empty
//   - tojMy68W (FriendInfoResponse) â€” populates FriendInfoList; per the IDA
//     dispatch table this is the "friend list" singleton used by other UIs
//     (general friend roster, friend detail screen).  Cheap to populate both
//     since we have the same source data.
//
// The Reinforcement picker UI almost certainly reads from one of these two
// singletons; sending both removes the ambiguity until we identify which.
// FriendInfo schema is in net/friends.kdl, ReinforcementInfo in
// net/reinforcement_info.kdl.

json FriendGetResp {
    doc "FriendGet (2o4axPIC) response â€” the friend list that populates the Reinforcement / squad-select picker.  Emits both xZH6EIQ7 (ReinforcementInfoList) and tojMy68W (FriendInfoList) with the same source data."

    field reinforce_info type="[ReinforcementInfo]" {
        key "xZH6EIQ7"
        doc "Friend list entries under the reinforce/helper picker key â€” matches the captured prod response shape."
    }

    field friend_info type="[FriendInfo]" {
        key "tojMy68W"
        doc "Same entries under the friend-info-list key â€” populates FriendInfoList for any UI that reads from there."
    }
}

